Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?raster:=20M1.1=20A2=20=E2=80=94=20Metal=20pipel?=
 =?UTF-8?q?ines=20and=20the=20float-depth=20finding?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

HardwareMetal exists: device, queue, and the rack's eight MSL
libraries, with graphics_pipeline mirroring the Vulkan
create_graphics_pipeline's descriptor shape — RGBA8 color target, the
placed-vertex input six Float4 attributes over a 24-float stride, the
depth+stencil pair on the same format, sample count 1. Cull/winding/
depth-test/blend stay per-command-encoder like Vulkan's dynamic
states; A3's encoders set the exact ones.

The raster's depth on Apple silicon is the float twin (D32F_S8): the
D24 UNORM stencil returns non-renderable in the descriptor validation
(MTL_PIXEL format 255 rejected), and the Vulkan path's float_depth
fallback covers the same requirement — depth_pixel_format keeps both,
the default key asks for the float.

default_pipelines_build_on_the_device: the two depth-variant pipelines
construct on the device and every rack shader hands back its function.
pixel_formats_match_the_vulkan_twins pins the four format constants.
